      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Row 106, Yucca gloriosa (Spanish dagger). Care: NC State, Missouri BG (its cached page is the 'Variegata' cultivar) and RHS agree on full sun, free drainage, drought tolerance and a slow-growing evergreen shrub. Size: RHS 1.5 to 2.5 m by 1.5 to 2.5 m after 10 to 20 years, NC State 1.8 to 4.9 m by 1.8 to 2.4 m, Missouri BG 'Variegata' 60 to 120 cm; 200 by 200 cm is a choice. Hardiness H5 is the RHS rating (NC State zone 7 to 11). Placement: NC State says it is often a container plant and can be a house plant; RHS gives coastal, courtyard and border uses. Toxicity: ASPCA genus page (Yucca spp.) says toxic to dogs, cats and horses, saponins, vomiting in dogs and cats; RHS says harmful to pets if eaten and a skin allergen (wear gloves); NC State tags it as a problem for dogs, cats and horses. Severity 2 for cats and dogs and 1 for skin are the agent's mapping; no source grades people eating it (NC State lists flowers and stems as edible). Es and it names are machine drafts."
      },
